WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:07.789 align:start position:0%
 
state  the military coup many young activists  came out onto the street to protest but  the military did not care they cracked  down on the protests causing many people  to want to leave I had to leave Kaya  state in September 2021 because I was  helping injured protesters and had  become too well known to the military  a few of my colleagues had been arrested  and I began to feel unsafe  the military went to some of the people  I had helped and wanted to know my name  and where I lived  I feared for my family's safety  so I decided to leave  when we arrived in mon state they passed  a new law forcing people to report and  register any guests or visitors  we were easily identifiable as strangers  as we looked different to the local  people so we continued on to miyawadi  then like but we faced the same problem  we had no choice but to cross the border  into Thailand I wrote to the unhcr in  December 2021 and had an interview with  them a few months later  but I heard nothing more so I applied to  Australia for Refugee status but I was  rejected that affected me a lot mentally  I have a wife and child but life is so  uncertain I don't know if or when the  Thai authorities will arrest and Deport  me I've sent letters to many embassies  including the U.S Canada and Norway  all of them tell me the same thing that  I need to have a un registration number  from the unhcr otherwise they can't help  me  in Mesa on the border I was arrested by  the Thai police I tried to call the  unhcr emergency number several times but  there was no response in the end I had  to pay a bribe to stop them from  deporting me I was very lucky I worry as  my parents and family members are still  in Myanmar  so I try to keep a low profile while  continuing to support the Freedom  Fighters  it's important not to draw too much  attention from the military  I send food and medical supplies from  Thailand  I try to help all civilians in Kaya  State regardless of which group they  belong to we're all human beings inside  Myanmar the revolution is taking longer  and it's not easy to raise funds I'm a  singer and I plan to upload some of my  songs to YouTube  once I get more than a million views  YouTube will pay me and I will donate  the money to the cause  [Music]

